phase P5
title Features
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** production code for the features outside the core, built from the Plans, one area at a
    time, each area's Specs written when it starts: entities, streams, record migration, multi-tab
    and sessions, host adapters, Stories, React and Next.js bindings, CLI outputs.

    **Starts when:** P15's completion audit passes (the core is done).

    **Verified by:** each area's suite slice, built and proven first (mutants, audit), then the area
    built against it; real-browser runs in Chrome and Safari; reviews. Coverage records in the
    owning Plan's verification.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task of the earliest area: an area without a proven slice gets
    its slice first; an area with one is built against it.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - each area's slice is proven and passes on production after its audit;
    - the user accepts the CLI outputs.

    **False pass:** a slice too lenient to fail.

    **Caught by:** the auditor's own mutants per area.

    **Gates:**

    - falsify per area;
    - the area's real-source path (a real `fetch`, EventSource or SDK call).

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a feature call only the user can make;
    - a guarantee change;
    - the user's acceptance of the CLI outputs, batched in one round.

    **User's read:** the CLI output mocks before that round; small API calls. Decisions: the CLI
    outputs, judged by the user; open feature calls in a Plan, judged by the user when they touch a
    name, guarantee or stated preference, otherwise by a reviewing agent.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:playbook-specify for each area's Specs;
    - skill:policy-verification for each slice;
    - skill:policy-testing: test first, module integration tests through the public interface (no
      unit tests of internals), and the scenarios that enforce each Invariant written before the code;
    - skill:playbook-build;
    - skill:check-runtime for the browser paths.
tasks
    T24
        title       Entity store
        status      draft
        priority    high
        description
            Prove the entities slice, then build the entity store on production from @plan.EntityDomains as merged
            (OD52).

            **Why now:** entities are the first P5 area, and the production runtime has no entity store yet.

            **Read first:** @plan.EntityDomains.O1, @plan.EntityDomains.D1,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md
            (the carry rows `a3b.*` and `audit-2.*`).

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a lenient slice → caught by the area audit's mutants.
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
        acceptance
            The entities slice is proven and passes on production.
    T25
        title       Streams
        status      draft
        priority    high
        description
            Prove the streams slice, then build streams on production as merged (OD53), with a real EventSource path.

            **Why now:** streams are a P5 area with no production code, and the suite carries open stream rows: C202
            eviction, jitter determinism, rule 70's wait per operation, T3's bound across two operations, `listen.none`.

            **Read first:** @plan.Operations.O4, code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the carry rows).

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a lenient slice → caught by the area audit's mutants.
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
        acceptance
            The streams slice is proven and passes on production, with a real EventSource path.
    T26
        title       Record migration
        status      draft
        priority    high
        description
            Prove the record migration slice, then build @plan.Persistence's migration on production as merged (OD54),
            against real storage shapes (IndexedDB structured clone, `localStorage` text).

            **Why now:** restore reads records from the first release, but nothing yet migrates a record whose shape has
            changed.

            **Read first:** @plan.Persistence.O4, @plan.Persistence.D1, @spec.Codec, @spec.Restore.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a lenient slice → caught by the area audit's mutants.
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
        acceptance
            The migration slice is proven and passes on production.
    T27
        title       Multi-tab and sessions
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Prove the multi-tab and sessions slice, then build multi-tab ownership and sessions from @plan.Runtime.

            **Why now:** nothing in production yet owns a scope across tabs or runs sessions, which
            @plan.Runtime.O7 and @plan.Persistence.O7 need.

            **Read first:** @plan.Runtime.O3, @plan.Runtime.O7, @plan.Persistence.O7.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** one-tab tests standing in for two → caught by a real two-tab browser
              run.
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
        acceptance
            The slice is proven and passes on production in real Chrome and Safari.
    T28
        title       Host adapters: IndexedDB and in-memory
        status      draft
        priority    high
        description
            Build the IndexedDB host adapter, meeting Safari's four requirements, and an in-memory adapter.

            **Why now:** production has no storage adapter, and a fake IndexedDB would hide Safari's behaviour.

            **Read first:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/safari/RESULTS.md, @plan.Persistence.O1,
            @plan.Persistence.D1, @spec.WriteAhead.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a fake standing in for IndexedDB → caught by skill:check-runtime in
              real Safari.
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries; real-browser runs.
        acceptance
            Both adapters pass the slice; the four Safari requirements hold in real Safari.
    T29
        title       Stories with flow story and flow trace
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Build @plan.Testing's Stories, `flow story list/describe/run` and `flow trace` on production.

            **Why now:** Stories are how tests and the example apps (P6) show behaviour, and the CLI has no story or
            trace
            commands yet.

            **Read first:** @plan.Testing.O1, @plan.Testing.O9, @plan.CommandLine.O2, @plan.CommandLine.O4.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a Story that re-executes on scrub → caught by the player tests (V9).
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries.
            - **Stops:** public entry-point names.
        acceptance
            The slice is proven and passes on production.
    T30
        title       React and Next.js bindings
        status      draft
        priority    high
        description
            Build the React and Next.js bindings from @plan.React and @plan.ServerRendering.

            **Why now:** UI is React and Next.js only, and production has no binding for either.

            **Read first:** @plan.React.O1, @plan.React.O2, @plan.ServerRendering.O1, @plan.ServerRendering.O4.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** tests in jsdom standing in for Next.js → caught by a real Next.js run.
            - **Gates:** the area's falsify entries.
            - **Stops:** public entry-point names; a large API change.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
